<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Chemistry Practice · Second Session 2027</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Titillium+Web:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root{--red:#e4002b;--red-d:#b80023;--ink:#212121;--mute:#5f5f5f;--line:#dcdcdc;--bg:#fff;--soft:#fdeef1;--dark:#4a4a4a;--ok:#1b7f45;--sh:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.16)}
*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0}
body{font-family:'Titillium Web',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:#fff;font-size:17px;line-height:1.45}
button{font:inherit;cursor:pointer}
.bar{background:var(--red);color:#fff;height:68px;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 clamp(16px,5vw,64px);gap:20px;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:5}
.bar .brand{font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.2px;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}
.bar .sp{flex:1}.bar .meta{font-weight:600;font-size:16px;opacity:.95}
.timer{background:#fff;color:var(--red);border-radius:6px;padding:4px 14px;font-weight:700;font-size:20px;min-width:96px;text-align:center;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.timer.low{background:var(--ink);color:#fff}
.wrap{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(16px,4vw,32px)}
h1{font-size:clamp(30px,4.5vw,46px);line-height:1.1;margin:48px 0 10px;font-weight:700}
h2{font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);text-align:center;margin:56px 0 0;font-weight:600}
h2:after{content:"";display:block;width:60px;height:2px;background:var(--red);margin:12px auto 36px}
.lead{color:var(--mute);margin:0;max-width:720px}
.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:24px;margin-bottom:72px}
.card{background:#fff;border-radius:4px;box-shadow:var(--sh);padding:20px 22px 18px;position:relative;cursor:pointer;text-align:left;border:0;min-height:128px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;transition:box-shadow .15s}
.card:hover{box-shadow:0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.24)}
.card h3{margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--red);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;padding-right:40px}
.card p{margin:0;color:var(--ink)}
.go{position:absolute;right:20px;bottom:16px;width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--red);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:16px;line-height:1}
.card.wide{grid-column:1/-1;background:var(--soft)}
.note{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--soft),#fff);padding:28px 0;margin-top:8px}
.note b{color:var(--red)}
.btn{border:0;border-radius:6px;padding:11px 22px;font-weight:600;font-size:17px;background:var(--dark);color:#fff}
.btn:hover{background:#333}.btn.red{background:var(--red)}.btn.red:hover{background:var(--red-d)}
.btn.line{background:#fff;color:var(--dark);border:1.5px solid var(--dark)}.btn.line:hover{background:#f3f3f3}
.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:default}
.quiz{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 290px;gap:28px;margin:32px 0 64px;align-items:start}
.qcard{background:#fff;border-radius:4px;box-shadow:var(--sh);padding:28px clamp(18px,3vw,36px)}
.qno{color:var(--red);font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;font-size:15px;margin-bottom:8px}
.stem{font-size:21px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 20px}
.qimg{max-width:100%;display:block;margin:0 0 20px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px}
.opt{display:flex;gap:14px;width:100%;text-align:left;background:#fff;border:1.5px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--ink)}
.opt:hover{border-color:#999}.opt .l{font-weight:700;color:var(--red);min-width:20px}
.opt.sel{border-color:var(--red);background:var(--soft)}
.nav{display:flex;gap:12px;margin-top:22px;align-items:center}.nav .sp{flex:1}
.side{background:#fff;border-radius:4px;box-shadow:var(--sh);padding:20px;position:sticky;top:88px}
.side h4{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:18px}.side small{color:var(--mute)}
.pal{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);gap:8px;margin:14px 0;max-height:340px;overflow-y:auto;overflow-x:hidden;padding:2px 8px 2px 2px}
.pal button,.st button{height:38px;border-radius:4px;border:1.5px solid var(--line);background:#f1f1f1;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink)}
.pal button.ans{background:var(--red);border-color:var(--red);color:#fff}.pal button.cur{outline:2.5px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:1px}
.legend{display:flex;gap:14px;font-size:14px;color:var(--mute);margin-bottom:16px}.legend i{display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;border-radius:2px;margin-right:5px;vertical-align:-1px;background:#d9d9d9}.legend i.a{background:var(--red)}
.res{text-align:center;margin:44px 0 8px}
.score{font-size:clamp(54px,9vw,88px);font-weight:700;color:var(--red);line-height:1}
.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px;margin:28px 0}
.stat{background:#fff;box-shadow:var(--sh);border-radius:4px;padding:16px;text-align:center}.stat b{display:block;font-size:30px}.stat span{color:var(--mute);font-size:15px}
.st{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(112px,1fr));gap:10px;margin:0 0 28px}
.st button{cursor:pointer;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:auto;padding:8px 4px;font-size:15px}
.st button small{font-weight:400;font-size:13px}
.st .c{background:#e9f6ee;border-color:var(--ok);color:var(--ok)}.st .w{background:var(--soft);border-color:var(--red);color:var(--red-d)}.st .u{color:var(--mute)}
.mask{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.55);display:grid;place-items:center;z-index:20;padding:16px}
.dlg{background:#fff;border-radius:6px;max-width:720px;width:100%;max-height:90vh;overflow:auto;padding:22px clamp(18px,3vw,30px);box-shadow:0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.35)}
.dlg .top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:6px}
.x{border:0;background:none;font-size:30px;line-height:1;color:var(--mute);padding:0 4px}
.dlg .opt{cursor:default;align-items:center}.dlg .opt:hover{border-color:var(--line)}
.dlg .opt span:nth-child(2){flex:1}.tag{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.4px;white-space:nowrap}
.dlg .opt.right{border-color:var(--ok);background:#e9f6ee}.dlg .opt.right .l,.dlg .opt.right .tag{color:var(--ok)}
.dlg .opt.wrong{border-color:var(--red);background:var(--soft)}.dlg .opt.wrong .tag{color:var(--red-d)}
@media(max-width:860px){.quiz{grid-template-columns:1fr}.side{position:static}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.bar .meta{display:none}}
</style></head>
<body><div id="app"></div>
<script>
const TOPICS=["Constitution of matter", "Structure of the atom", "Periodic table of elements", "Chemical bond", "Fundamentals of inorganic chemistry", "Solutions", "Chemical reactions and stoichiometry", "Equilibria in aqueous solution", "Elements of chemical kinetics and catalysis", "Oxidation and reduction", "Acids and bases", "Fundamentals of organic chemistry", "Ideal gas laws"],DATA=[{"n":1,"t":13,"q":"What volume, in litres, of oxygen gas is required to react with 2 litres of methane according to the reaction CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O, measured under the same conditions of temperature and pressure?","o":["4","2","1","5","6"]},{"n":2,"t":7,"q":"Consider one mole of nitrogen with molecular formula N₂. If its mass is 28 g, we can state that:","o":["the atomic weight of nitrogen is 14 amu","one mole of nitrogen under standard conditions occupies 224 litres","one nitrogen molecule weighs 28 grams","the atomic mass of nitrogen is 28","one mole of N₂ molecules weighs 14"]},{"n":3,"t":4,"q":"On the basis of its characteristics, we can state that the PI₃ molecule has:","o":["trigonal-pyramidal geometry","trigonal-planar geometry","cubic geometry","square-pyramidal geometry","hexagonal geometry"]},{"n":4,"t":5,"q":"Why does spreading salt on roads prevent ice from forming in winter?","o":["The presence of salt lowers the freezing point of water","The salt dissolves in the water present, releasing heat","The melting point of water rises because of the presence of salt","The hygroscopic salt absorbs water, preventing ice formation","The salt alters the molecular structure of water, thereby preventing ice formation"]},{"n":5,"t":11,"q":"If a base is added to an acidic solution:","o":["the pH increases","the pH remains unchanged","the result cannot be predicted","the pKa increases","the pKa decreases"]},{"n":6,"t":13,"q":"What volume is occupied by 1.806 × 10²⁴ molecules of hydrogen chloride at 0°C and 1 atm?","o":["67.2 litres","6.7 litres","33.6 litres","2.24 litres","448.0 litres"]},{"n":7,"t":5,"q":"The empirical formula of calcium phosphate is:","o":["Ca₃(PO₄)₂","3Ca(PO₄)₂","Ca₃(HPO₄)₂","Ca₃(PO)₅","Ca₃(P₅O)₄"]},{"n":8,"t":11,"q":"The pH scale ranges from 0 to 14. A solution with pH = 12 is:","o":["strongly basic","strongly acidic","at neutral pH","at physiological pH","rich in H⁺ ions"]},{"n":9,"t":1,"q":"During solidification, a substance changes from the liquid state to the solid state. The process occurs with:","o":["release of heat","absorption of energy","a decrease in the number of moles","an increase in the number of moles","a decrease in weight"]},{"n":10,"t":5,"q":"Which of the following chemical formulae is NOT possible?","o":["Ca(BO₃)₂","KMnO₄","NaClO₄","Ca(H₂PO₄)₂","PbCO₃"]},{"n":11,"t":5,"q":"Identify the chemical formula of the hypobromite ion.","o":["BrO⁻","Br₂O⁻","BrO₂⁻","HBrO⁻","BrO₃⁻"]},{"n":12,"t":4,"q":"Which of the following pairs consists of molecules that both have trigonal-planar structures according to Valence Shell Electron Pair Repulsion (VSEPR) theory?","o":["BH₃; SO₃","NH₃; BCl₃","SO₂; H₂O","PCl₃; CH₄","NH₃; PH₃"]},{"n":13,"t":2,"q":"In an atom in its ground state, which energy level do electrons tend to occupy first?","o":["The level of lowest energy and shortest distance from the nucleus","The level of highest energy and greatest distance from the nucleus","They tend to be distributed randomly among the orbitals around the nucleus","The level of the first available hybrid orbital","The level of the lowest-energy molecular orbital"]},{"n":14,"t":6,"q":"Electrolytes are substances:","o":["that dissociate into ions in water","that are insoluble in water","that are soluble in fats","that do not dissociate into ions in water","that never conduct electric current in the solid state"]},{"n":15,"t":11,"q":"Which of the following characteristics must an acid have in order to be defined as monoprotic?","o":["It must be able to transfer only one hydrogen ion to a base","It must be a binary acid","It must be a binary compound","It must be a compound of hydrogen and an alkali metal","It must be able to react only with strong bases"]},{"n":16,"t":12,"q":"The oxidation of an aldehyde produces:","o":["an acid","an amide","an ether","a halohydrin","a peroxide"]},{"n":17,"t":3,"q":"The periodic table is divided into rows and columns according to the characteristics of the elements. The rows are also called:","o":["periods","blocks","alkali metals","halogens","groups"]},{"n":18,"t":5,"q":"Identify the traditional name of the compound Cu(NO₃)₂.","o":["cupric nitrate","cuprous nitrate","cupric nitrite","cuprous nitrite","cupric ammonium"]},{"n":19,"t":5,"q":"Which of the following empirical formulae identifies magnesium hydrogen phosphate?","o":["MgHPO₄","MgHPO₃","MgH₂PO₄","Mg₂HPO₄","Mg₃(PO₄)₂"]},{"n":20,"t":11,"q":"Given a solution with pH = 8, we can state that it is:","o":["weakly basic","at physiological pH","at acidic pH","at neutral pH","devoid of anions, if it is an aqueous solution"]},{"n":21,"t":7,"q":"What is the numerical value of Avogadro's constant?","o":["6.02 × 10²³","1.66 × 10²³","0.602 × 10⁻²⁴","1.66 × 10⁻²⁷","60.2 × 10²³"]},{"n":22,"t":4,"q":"The angle between sp hybrid orbitals is:","o":["180°","122°","112°","98°","none of the other alternatives is correct"]},{"n":23,"t":11,"q":"NH₄⁺ is the conjugate acid of which base?","o":["NH₃","HCl","NaOH","NH₂⁻","N(OH)₃"]},{"n":24,"t":10,"q":"Which oxidation state or states does fluorine exhibit in its compounds?","o":["−1","All integer values from −1 to −7","All integer values from −1 to +7","−1, −3, −5, −7","−1, +1, +3, +5, +7"]},{"n":25,"t":3,"q":"Ionisation energy is a characteristic of all elements in the periodic table. Which of the following elements has the highest first ionisation energy?","o":["F","Mg","Li","Sr","Br"]},{"n":26,"t":5,"q":"The reaction of non-metals with oxygen leads to the formation of:","o":["acid anhydrides","esters","hydroxides","alkenes","halohydrins"]},{"n":27,"t":11,"q":"According to Brønsted theory, CO₃²⁻ and H⁺ can both be considered bases. Their conjugate acids are:","o":["HCO₃⁻ and H₂","HCO₃ and H⁺","HCO₃ and H₃O⁺","H₂CO₃ and OH⁻","CO₃²⁻ and H⁺"]},{"n":28,"t":7,"q":"What is the mass of 3.011 × 10²³ formula units of MgF₂? (Ar of magnesium = 24.3 u; Ar of fluorine = 19.0)","o":["31.15 g","62.3 g","43.3 g","21.65 g","33.8 g"]},{"n":29,"t":4,"q":"Triple bonds consist of:","o":["one σ bond and two π bonds","three coordinate bonds","two ionic bonds and one non-polar covalent bond","two polar covalent bonds and one non-polar covalent bond","two σ bonds and one π bond"]},{"n":30,"t":11,"q":"Which of the following mathematical expressions defines pH?","o":["pH = −log[H⁺]","pH = ln[OH⁻]","pH = −log[OH⁻]","pH = log[H⁺]/log[OH⁻]","pH = −log[H⁺]7"]},{"n":31,"t":12,"q":"Which of the following statements about saponification is correct?","o":["It is an ester hydrolysis reaction","It is the synthesis reaction of triglycerides","It is a base-synthesis reaction","It is the reduction reaction of fatty acids","It is the reaction that forms phospholipids"]},{"n":32,"t":11,"q":"What is the traditional name of the phosphorus oxyacid with formula H₄P₂O₇?","o":["pyrophosphoric acid","metaphosphoric acid","orthophosphorous acid","metaphosphorous acid","orthophosphoric acid"]},{"n":33,"t":11,"q":"Which of the following properties changes only slightly in a buffer solution after the addition of a small amount of strong base?","o":["pH","electronegativity","the triple point","the boiling point of the solvent","specific volume"]},{"n":34,"t":4,"q":"The bond formed in the oxygen molecule O₂ is:","o":["a non-polar covalent bond","an ionic bond","oxygen does not exist in molecular form","a metallic bond","a dipole–dipole interaction"]},{"n":35,"t":12,"q":"When can a carbon atom be a stereocentre?","o":["When it has four different substituents","When it is sp²-hybridised","When it is part of a double bond","When it has at least two identical substituents","When it is bonded to at least two hydrogen atoms"]},{"n":36,"t":4,"q":"Which of the following compounds contains NO covalent triple bond?","o":["Na₂Cr₂O₇","N₂","HCN","H₂C₂","HSCN"]},{"n":37,"t":1,"q":"Which of the following changes of state occurs only when heat is supplied?","o":["Melting","Crystallisation","Solidification","Deposition","Condensation"]},{"n":38,"t":4,"q":"How many non-bonding electrons are present in the outermost shell of one nitrogen atom in the N₂H₄ molecule?","o":["2","3","4","1","5"]},{"n":39,"t":12,"q":"In organic chemistry, the suffix \"-one\" is used for:","o":["ketones","chains containing more than 12 atoms","ethers","acids","sugars consisting of more than two rings"]},{"n":40,"t":2,"q":"If an element has mass number 32 and atomic number 15, we can state that it has:","o":["15 protons and 17 neutrons","at least 1 radioactive isotope","more protons than neutrons","equal numbers of protons and neutrons","17 protons and 15 neutrons"]},{"n":41,"t":3,"q":"Beryllium is:","o":["none of the alternatives is correct","a noble gas","an alkali metal","a lanthanide","a halogen"]},{"n":42,"t":7,"q":"At 20°C and 1 atm and without the use of catalysts, identify the products of the chemical reaction between the following reactants: H₂SO₄ + Mg(OH)₂ →","o":["MgSO₄ + 2H₂O","MgSO₄ + 2H₂","Mg + H₂O + SO₃","MgS + 2H₂O","Mg + H₂O + SO₄"]},{"n":43,"t":4,"q":"What type of bonds characterise the primary structure of proteins?","o":["Peptide bonds","Hydrogen bonds","Non-polar covalent bonds","Ester bonds","Thioester bonds"]},{"n":44,"t":7,"q":"What is the mass of 9.033 × 10²³ molecules of H₃BO₃? (Ar of boron = 10.8 u)","o":["92.7 g","30.9 g","61.8 g","14.98 × 10⁻²⁴ g","44.7 g"]},{"n":45,"t":3,"q":"Li, Na and K belong to the first group (IA). What characterises these elements?","o":["They have one electron in the outermost s orbital","They have higher electronegativity than the compounds of group IIA","They have one electron in the outermost px orbital","They do not react with water","They cannot be oxidised"]},{"n":46,"t":2,"q":"What determines the chemical properties of the elements?","o":["Atomic number","The periodic table","Mole fraction","Specific weight","The ratio of protons to neutrons"]},{"n":47,"t":7,"q":"A mass of hydrogen bromide molecules, expressed in grams, is equal to three times the sum of the relative atomic mass of bromine and the relative atomic mass of hydrogen. How many molecules constitute this mass? (Ar of bromine = 80 u)","o":["1.806 × 10²⁴","it contains no molecules because it is an ionic compound","6.02 × 10²³","2.43 × 10²²","243.01 × 10²³"]},{"n":48,"t":4,"q":"The compound with empirical formula MgBr₂ is:","o":["ionic","composed of molecules containing two polar covalent bonds","composed of molecules containing two non-polar covalent bonds","composed of molecules containing two covalent double bonds","based on metallic bonds joining the three atoms"]},{"n":49,"t":6,"q":"The elevation of the boiling point of an aqueous solution depends:","o":["only on the number of solute particles in solution","only on the chemical nature of the solute","only on the osmotic pressure","only on van der Waals forces","only on latent heat"]},{"n":50,"t":5,"q":"In the traditional nomenclature of oxides, the suffix -ic indicates the oxide:","o":["in which the metal has the higher oxidation state","in which the metal has oxidation state +1","with the higher oxygen content","in which oxygen is absent","in which the metal forms a non-polar covalent bond with oxygen"]},{"n":51,"t":4,"q":"Which of the following molecules is polar?","o":["CHCl₃","CH₄","CO₂","N₂","CCl₄"]},{"n":52,"t":4,"q":"Identify which of the following elements can form ionic bonds with chlorine.","o":["Mg","P","C","Se","F"]},{"n":53,"t":10,"q":"Identify the chemical formula in which sulfur has oxidation state +4 and iron has oxidation state +3.","o":["Fe₂(SO₃)₃","Fe₂(SO)₃","Fe₂(SO₄)₃","FeS","Fe(SO₃)₃"]},{"n":54,"t":12,"q":"Indicate which of the following is the formula of butane:","o":[